  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "LC002 no longer reports a misleading \"redundant\" materialization when the source is a keyed (ToDictionary) or grouped (ToLookup) materializer. A trailing ToList after ToDictionary/ToLookup is a genuine shape change (it yields a List of KeyValuePair / List of IGrouping), not a redundant re-materialization, so it is now left quiet — matching the existing de-duplicating-set exclusion. Genuinely redundant non-keyed collapses such as ToArray().ToList() still report and fix.",
